UNIT sign
KIND STATE
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
# Deterministic ONLY when the input pins the date and passes explicit credentials (see SEAM CONTRACT).
# genInputs guarantees both, so under-the-generator every output is a pure function of the input tuple.

SIG sign(request: object, credentials: object) -> request   # the SAME request object, mutated in place
  # request:     { path?, body?, host?|hostname?, method?, headers?, service?, region?, port?,
  #               signQuery?, doNotModifyHeaders?, doNotEncodePath?,
  #               extraHeadersToInclude?, extraHeadersToIgnore? }
  # credentials: { accessKeyId, secretAccessKey, sessionToken? }
  # module.exports.sign(request, credentials) == new RequestSigner(request, credentials).sign()

DEPENDS-ON crypto (HMAC-SHA256, SHA256), url.parse (only when request is a STRING — OUT-OF-SCOPE here),
           querystring.parse / querystring.stringify, an LRU signing-key cache (BEHAVIOR-NEUTRAL — pure
           memoization of the kCredentials derivation; identical output with or without it).

# ============================================================================================
# SEAM CONTRACT (determinism boundary — the generator MUST keep the unit above this seam)
# ============================================================================================
# Two ambient reads make sign() non-deterministic. genInputs eliminates BOTH:
#
# SEAM 1 — CLOCK. If no usable date is supplied, sign() reads `new Date()`.
#   * Non-signQuery, non-doNotModifyHeaders: datetime <- headers['X-Amz-Date'] || headers['x-amz-date']
#       if present, ELSE headers['X-Amz-Date'] is SET to getDateTime() which reads
#       `new Date(headers.Date || headers.date || new Date)`.
#       => DETERMINISTIC iff headers carry 'X-Amz-Date'/'x-amz-date' OR a 'Date'/'date' header.
#   * signQuery: datetime <- query['X-Amz-Date'] if present (parsed from the PATH query string),
#       ELSE query['X-Amz-Date'] is SET to getDateTime() (which reads new Date()).
#       NOTE: in signQuery mode an 'X-Amz-Date' *header* is IGNORED for the datetime — the date must be
#       in the PATH's query string (e.g. path:'/...?X-Amz-Date=20150830T123600Z').
#   * doNotModifyHeaders: the whole header-defaulting block is SKIPPED, so `this.datetime` is NEVER set
#       from X-Amz-Date. getDateTime() then reads `new Date(headers.Date||headers.date||new Date)`.
#       => DETERMINISTIC iff a 'Date'/'date' header is present. An 'X-Amz-Date' header does NOT pin it.
#   The deployed wrapper passes the real clock; the verified core is the function-of-(pinned date) above.
#
# SEAM 2 — ENV. If `credentials` is falsy, sign() reads process.env (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, ...).
#   genInputs ALWAYS passes explicit credentials, so the env is never read.
#
# OUT-OF-SCOPE / non-round-trippable (DOCUMENTED, never emitted by genInputs):
#   - request as a STRING (url.parse path)        - Buffer / non-string body
#   - undefined/absent credentials (env read)     - unpinned clock (new Date())
#   - any header value that is undefined/NaN/boxed - these poison the JSON codec round-trip

# ============================================================================================
# BEHAVIOR — exact ordered pipeline. sign() == prepareRequest(); then sign-finalize; then formatPath.
# ============================================================================================

# ---- CONSTRUCTION (RequestSigner constructor) ----
# C1. If request is a string -> url.parse(request). (OUT-OF-SCOPE; generator never emits.)
# C2. headers = request.headers = (request.headers || {}).   (mutates request: ensures a headers obj)
# C3. service/region inference (only if not explicitly given): hostParts = matchHost(
#       request.hostname || request.host || headers.Host || headers.host).  See matchHost below.
# C4. this.request = request; this.credentials = credentials || defaultCredentials()  [ENV seam].
# C5. this.service = request.service || hostParts[0] || ''
#     this.region  = request.region  || hostParts[1] || 'us-east-1'
# C6. if (this.service === 'email') this.service = 'ses'     # SES domain != service name
# C7. if (!request.method && request.body) request.method = 'POST'     # body implies POST default
# C8. HOST defaulting: if neither headers.Host nor headers.host set:
#        headers.Host = request.hostname || request.host || createHost()
#        if (request.port) headers.Host += ':' + request.port
# C9. if (!request.hostname && !request.host) request.hostname = headers.Host || headers.host
# C10. isCodeCommitGit = (service==='codecommit' && method==='GIT')   # OUT-OF-SCOPE (GIT method)
# C11. extraHeadersToIgnore  = request.extraHeadersToIgnore  || {}    (null-proto)
#      extraHeadersToInclude = request.extraHeadersToInclude || {}    (null-proto)

# ---- matchHost(host) -> [service, region] ----
#   match = (host||'').match(/([^.]+)\.(?:([^.]*)\.)?amazonaws\.com(\.cn)?$/)
#   hostParts = (match||[]).slice(1,3)        # [first-label, optional-second-label]
#   if hostParts[1] === 'es' || hostParts[1] === 'aoss': hostParts.reverse()   # ES/AOSS swap
#   if hostParts[1] === 's3': hostParts = ['s3','us-east-1']
#   else: for i in 0,1: if /^s3-/.test(hostParts[i]): { region=hostParts[i].slice(3); service='s3'; break }
#   Examples (VERIFIED):
#     s3.amazonaws.com                       -> service s3,       region us-east-1
#     iam.amazonaws.com                      -> service iam,      region us-east-1
#     dynamodb.us-west-2.amazonaws.com       -> service dynamodb, region us-west-2
#     examplebucket.s3.amazonaws.com         -> service s3,       region us-east-1
#     email.us-east-1.amazonaws.com          -> service ses (via C6 from 'email'), region us-east-1
#     search-foo.us-east-1.es.amazonaws.com  -> service es,       region us-east-1   (reversed)
#     dynamodb.cn-north-1.amazonaws.com.cn   -> service dynamodb, region cn-north-1
#     s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com             -> service s3,       region eu-west-1
#   A non-amazonaws host yields hostParts effectively ['',''] -> service '', region 'us-east-1' unless
#   request.service/request.region override.

# ---- isSingleRegion() (used by createHost only) ----
#   true if (service in {s3,sdb} && region==='us-east-1') OR
#           service in {cloudfront, ls, route53, iam, importexport, sts}.
# ---- createHost() ----
#   region = isSingleRegion() ? '' : '.'+this.region ; subdomain = service==='ses'?'email':service
#   return subdomain + region + '.amazonaws.com'

# ============================================================================================
# prepareRequest()  — runs parsePath() then branches on signQuery
# ============================================================================================
# parsePath():
#   path = request.path || '/'
#   if /[^0-9A-Za-z;,/?:@&=+$\-_.!~*'()#%]/.test(path):  path = encodeURI(decodeURI(path))   # re-encode
#   queryIx = path.indexOf('?'); if queryIx>=0: query = querystring.parse(path.slice(queryIx+1));
#                                                path = path.slice(0,queryIx)   else query = null
#   parsedPath = { path, query }
#
# BRANCH A — request.signQuery truthy (query-string signing):
#   parsedPath.query = query = parsedPath.query || {}
#   if credentials.sessionToken: query['X-Amz-Security-Token'] = sessionToken
#   if service==='s3' && !query['X-Amz-Expires']: query['X-Amz-Expires'] = 86400
#   if query['X-Amz-Date']: datetime = query['X-Amz-Date']   else query['X-Amz-Date'] = getDateTime() [CLOCK seam]
#   query['X-Amz-Algorithm']    = 'AWS4-HMAC-SHA256'
#   query['X-Amz-Credential']   = accessKeyId + '/' + credentialString()
#   query['X-Amz-SignedHeaders']= signedHeaders()
#   (Authorization header is NOT touched in this branch.)
#
# BRANCH B — header signing (default):
#   if (!doNotModifyHeaders && !isCodeCommitGit):
#     if body && no Content-Type/content-type:  headers['Content-Type']='application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8'
#     if body && no Content-Length/content-length: headers['Content-Length']=Buffer.byteLength(body)  # a NUMBER
#     if sessionToken && no X-Amz-Security-Token/x-amz-security-token: headers['X-Amz-Security-Token']=sessionToken
#     if service==='s3' && no X-Amz-Content-Sha256/x-amz-content-sha256: headers['X-Amz-Content-Sha256']=SHA256hex(body||'')
#     if headers['X-Amz-Date']||headers['x-amz-date']: datetime = that value
#        else: headers['X-Amz-Date'] = getDateTime()   [CLOCK seam]
#   delete headers.Authorization; delete headers.authorization   # ALWAYS (even under doNotModifyHeaders)

# ============================================================================================
# sign-finalize (RequestSigner.prototype.sign)
# ============================================================================================
#   if (!parsedPath) prepareRequest()      # already run above
#   if signQuery: parsedPath.query['X-Amz-Signature'] = signature()
#   else:         request.headers.Authorization = authHeader()
#   request.path = formatPath()
#   return request

# ---- getDateTime() ----   (memoized in this.datetime)
#   if !datetime: date = new Date(headers.Date || headers.date || new Date)
#                 datetime = date.toISOString().replace(/[:\-]|\.\d{3}/g,'')
#                 # i.e. "2015-08-30T12:36:00.000Z" -> "20150830T123600Z"
#                 if isCodeCommitGit: datetime = datetime.slice(0,-1)   # strip trailing Z (OUT-OF-SCOPE)
#   return datetime
# ---- getDate() = getDateTime().substr(0,8)    e.g. "20150830"
# ---- credentialString() = [getDate(), region, service, 'aws4_request'].join('/')
#        e.g. "20150830/us-east-1/iam/aws4_request"

# ---- authHeader() ----   (header-signing branch only)
#   return  'AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=' + accessKeyId + '/' + credentialString()
#         + ', SignedHeaders=' + signedHeaders()
#         + ', Signature=' + signature()
#   (NB the three pieces are joined with ', ' — comma SPACE.)

# ---- signature() -> hex ----
#   date = getDate(); cacheKey = [secretAccessKey, date, region, service].join()   # ','-joined; LRU only
#   kDate        = HMAC( 'AWS4'+secretAccessKey , date )           # raw bytes
#   kRegion      = HMAC( kDate , region )
#   kService     = HMAC( kRegion , service )
#   kCredentials = HMAC( kService , 'aws4_request' )
#   return HMAC( kCredentials , stringToSign() ).hex
#   (LRU cache memoizes kCredentials by cacheKey — output-identical; treat as pure.)

# ---- stringToSign() ----
#   return [ 'AWS4-HMAC-SHA256', getDateTime(), credentialString(), SHA256hex(canonicalString()) ].join('\n')

# ============================================================================================
# canonicalString()  — the heart; flags derived from service
# ============================================================================================
#   pathStr   = parsedPath.path ; query = parsedPath.query ; headers = request.headers
#   normalizePath        = service !== 's3'
#   decodePath           = service === 's3' || request.doNotEncodePath
#   decodeSlashesInPath  = service === 's3'
#   firstValOnly         = service === 's3'
#
#   bodyHash:
#     if service==='s3' && signQuery:  bodyHash = 'UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD'
#     elif isCodeCommitGit:            bodyHash = ''                       (OUT-OF-SCOPE)
#     else: bodyHash = headers['X-Amz-Content-Sha256'] || headers['x-amz-content-sha256']
#                      || SHA256hex(body || '')
#
#   QUERY canonicalization (if query):
#     reducedQuery = {} ; for key in Object.keys(query):
#        if !key: skip
#        reducedQuery[ encodeRfc3986Full(key) ] = Array.isArray(query[key])
#             ? (firstValOnly ? query[key][0] : query[key]) : query[key]
#     encodedQueryPieces = []
#     for key in Object.keys(reducedQuery).sort():
#        if not Array: push( key + '=' + encodeRfc3986Full(value) )
#        else: value.map(encodeRfc3986Full).sort().forEach(v => push(key + '=' + v))
#     queryStr = encodedQueryPieces.join('&')
#     (Keys sorted ASCII; array values individually encoded then sorted; S3 keeps only first value.)
#
#   PATH canonicalization (only if pathStr !== '/'):
#     if normalizePath: pathStr = pathStr.replace(/\/{2,}/g,'/')           # collapse repeated slashes
#     pathStr = split('/').reduce(path, piece):
#         if normalizePath && piece==='..': path.pop()
#         elif !normalizePath || piece !== '.':
#             if decodePath: piece = decodeURIComponent(piece.replace(/\+/g,' '))
#             path.push( encodeRfc3986Full(piece) )
#       join('/')
#     if pathStr[0] !== '/': pathStr = '/' + pathStr
#     if decodeSlashesInPath: pathStr = pathStr.replace(/%2F/g,'/')        # S3: restore literal '/'
#
#   return [ request.method || 'GET', pathStr, queryStr, canonicalHeaders()+'\n',
#            signedHeaders(), bodyHash ].join('\n')

# ---- encodeRfc3986Full(s) = encodeRfc3986(encodeURIComponent(s)) ----
#   encodeRfc3986(u) = u.replace(/[!'()*]/g, c => '%' + c.charCodeAt(0).toString(16).toUpperCase())
#   i.e. percent-encode, then ALSO percent-encode the 5 chars ! ' ( ) * (which encodeURIComponent leaves).

# ============================================================================================
# canonicalHeaders()  vs  signedHeaders()  ===  *** THE DESYNC — PRESERVE EXACTLY ***
# ============================================================================================
# HEADERS_TO_IGNORE (lowercased keys, value true):
#   authorization, connection, x-amzn-trace-id, user-agent, expect, presigned-expires, range
#
# canonicalHeaders()  — builds the SIGNED CANONICAL-HEADERS BLOCK:
#   take Object.keys(headers)
#     .filter( key => HEADERS_TO_IGNORE[key.toLowerCase()] == null )   # ONLY HEADERS_TO_IGNORE; NO override
#     .sort( (a,b) => a.toLowerCase() < b.toLowerCase() ? -1 : 1 )     # case-insensitive sort
#     .map( key => key.toLowerCase() + ':' + trimAll(headers[key]) )
#     .join('\n')
#   trimAll(h) = h.toString().trim().replace(/\s+/g,' ')               # numeric values coerced via toString
#   *** canonicalHeaders DOES NOT consult extraHeadersToInclude OR extraHeadersToIgnore. ***
#
# signedHeaders()  — builds the SignedHeaders LIST:
#   take Object.keys(headers).map(k => k.toLowerCase())
#     .filter( key => extraHeadersToInclude[key]                       # <-- INCLUDE override applied HERE
#                     || (HEADERS_TO_IGNORE[key] == null && !extraHeadersToIgnore[key]) )
#     .sort().join(';')
#   *** signedHeaders DOES honor extraHeadersToInclude AND extraHeadersToIgnore. ***
#
# *** CONSEQUENCE (THE DESYNC — DO NOT "FIX") ***
#   With extraHeadersToInclude = {'user-agent':1} and a 'user-agent' header present:
#     - signedHeaders() FORCES 'user-agent' INTO the SignedHeaders list.
#     - canonicalHeaders() STILL FILTERS 'user-agent' OUT (it is in HEADERS_TO_IGNORE; no include-override).
#   => The SignedHeaders list claims 'user-agent' was signed, but the canonical-headers block OMITS it.
#      The signature is computed over the block WITHOUT user-agent. This is observably what real aws4 emits.
#   A "corrected" reconstruction that ALSO adds user-agent to the block produces a DIFFERENT, WRONG
#   signature and will be REJECTED by the differential. REPRODUCE THE DESYNC.
#
#   Symmetric note: extraHeadersToIgnore removes a header from the SignedHeaders LIST but, since
#   canonicalHeaders ignores extraHeadersToIgnore, the header (if not in HEADERS_TO_IGNORE) STILL appears
#   in the canonical-headers BLOCK — the mirror-image desync. (Anchor 2 below.)

# ---- formatPath() ----
#   path = parsedPath.path ; query = parsedPath.query
#   if !query: return path
#   if query[''] != null: delete query['']                         # services reject empty query keys
#   return path + '?' + encodeRfc3986( querystring.stringify(query) )
#   (Output path query is querystring.stringify'd then encodeRfc3986'd — a DIFFERENT, looser encoding than
#    the canonical queryStr; the output path may keep original key order / un-sorted, e.g. '/?b=2&a=1'.)

# ============================================================================================
# GOLDEN ANCHORS (VERIFIED against real aws4@1.12.0 — blind re-emitter MUST reproduce these)
# ============================================================================================
# ANCHOR 1 — THE INCLUDE DESYNC:
#   sign({ host:'iam.amazonaws.com', method:'GET', path:'/',
#          extraHeadersToInclude:{'user-agent':1},
#          headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z','User-Agent':'myagent/1.0'} },
#        { accessKeyId:'AKIDEXAMPLE',
#          secretAccessKey:'wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY' })
#   inferred service=iam region=us-east-1 ; Host added = iam.amazonaws.com
#   canonicalString (note BLOCK omits user-agent, LIST includes it):
#     "GET\n/\n\nhost:iam.amazonaws.com\nx-amz-date:20150830T123600Z\n\nhost;user-agent;x-amz-date\n"
#     + SHA256hex("") where SHA256hex("")=e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
#   RESULT headers.Authorization (EXACT):
#     AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=AKIDEXAMPLE/20150830/us-east-1/iam/aws4_request, SignedHeaders=host;user-agent;x-amz-date, Signature=0d5803a8a3f4f1ece0955648b12520c41f06ce33b3a3a908547e979e9e596b02
#   (Sanity: the consistent-block variant would give 72b260a126f769ac687ae74faf5c77bce6c5724bef6d980a929a31301ba77705 — WRONG.)
#
# ANCHOR 2 — extraHeadersToIgnore (LIST drops it; BLOCK keeps it):
#   sign({ host:'iam.amazonaws.com', method:'GET', path:'/',
#          extraHeadersToIgnore:{'x-custom':1},
#          headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z','X-Custom':'foo'} }, <same creds>)
#   SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-date  (x-custom dropped from list) BUT block contains x-custom:foo.
#   Signature=2010d0fbfba835b750622701b4a827333cb12833a5c8aa086159ec0b549e8dfd
#
# ANCHOR 3 — sessionToken (header signing):
#   sign({host:'iam.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/',headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z'}},
#        {accessKeyId:'AKIDEXAMPLE',secretAccessKey:'wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY',sessionToken:'SESSIONTOKEN123'})
#   adds header X-Amz-Security-Token:SESSIONTOKEN123 ; SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-date;x-amz-security-token
#   Signature=415fb1f2d587baa66f362a5b6779b1ac98a083e41685cc6b1860a3f458172c51
#
# ANCHOR 4 — POST body (dynamodb, no token):
#   sign({host:'dynamodb.us-east-1.amazonaws.com',method:'POST',path:'/',body:'Action=Foo',
#         headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z'}}, <creds no token>)
#   adds Content-Type:'application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8', Content-Length:10 (number)
#   SignedHeaders=content-length;content-type;host;x-amz-date
#   Signature=0dfede1ba715f4b3e567de9ff592e3b9253c6a60fb50ae7ca1a9d4b58c701374
#
# ANCHOR 5 — s3 PUT body (x-amz-content-sha256):
#   sign({host:'examplebucket.s3.amazonaws.com',method:'PUT',path:'/test.txt',body:'hello',
#         headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z'}}, <creds no token>)
#   adds X-Amz-Content-Sha256 = SHA256hex('hello') = 2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824
#   SignedHeaders=content-length;content-type;host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date
#   Signature=b29d29ef272af89e47ac61544fd49ea51ae232db2dd14b89eb727fca8b65cc87
#
# ANCHOR 6 — signQuery (date pinned IN PATH QUERY):
#   sign({host:'iam.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/?Action=ListUsers&X-Amz-Date=20150830T123600Z',
#         signQuery:true, headers:{}}, <creds no token>)
#   NO Authorization header. request.path (EXACT):
#     /?Action=ListUsers&X-Amz-Date=20150830T123600Z&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=AKIDEXAMPLE%2F20150830%2Fus-east-1%2Fiam%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Signature=4a77587665679b48774eee13fb82bbcf400e26b0691e71716ad4c9f2a6032724
#
# ANCHOR 7 — s3 signQuery (X-Amz-Expires=86400, UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD):
#   sign({host:'examplebucket.s3.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/test.txt?X-Amz-Date=20150830T123600Z',
#         signQuery:true, headers:{}}, <creds no token>)
#   request.path (EXACT):
#     /test.txt?X-Amz-Date=20150830T123600Z&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=AKIDEXAMPLE%2F20150830%2Fus-east-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Signature=3e06918c20a2f376548699c2a3312dbf05d1d2c561e98a4718b4a2e3aece2e88
#
# ANCHOR 8 — doNotModifyHeaders (Date header pins clock; NO defaulting; only Authorization added/deleted):
#   sign({host:'iam.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/',doNotModifyHeaders:true,
#         headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z','Date':'Sun, 30 Aug 2015 12:36:00 GMT'}}, <creds no token>)
#   Host added (host defaulting is in the constructor, NOT gated by doNotModifyHeaders).
#   getDateTime reads the Date header -> 20150830T123600Z. SignedHeaders=date;host;x-amz-date
#   Signature=91d8c0d2717c5c25e1b56df90048664849fe7d6bd75b23b9b11e15afca37b11c
#
# ANCHOR 9 — path normalization + array query (non-s3):
#   sign({host:'iam.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/foo//bar/../baz?b=2&a=1',
#         headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z'}}, <creds no token>)
#   canonical path = /foo/baz (collapse '//', resolve '..'); canonical query sorts a<b: a=1&b=2.
#   Signature=57648242e9e101a136c55af118ea891408b8f49b081a6744587577a3a41b6322
#   request.path (output) = /foo//bar/../baz?b=2&a=1   (formatPath does NOT normalize path; re-stringifies query)
#
# ANCHOR 10 — s3 path (NO normalization, slashes preserved):
#   sign({host:'examplebucket.s3.amazonaws.com',method:'GET',path:'/foo//bar/../baz',
#         headers:{'X-Amz-Date':'20150830T123600Z'}}, <creds no token>)
#   Signature=ebb933b3071b97265a035c1e237a7357341084437d16a69acbef619e09c55f27

ORACLE value -> oracle.json
  # Observable = { result, post } per call. result is the returned (== mutated) request; post is the
  # mutated request object (they are the same reference at runtime). The harness deep-clones each input
  # tuple (structuredClone) BEFORE the call so mutation cannot leak between cases, and snapshots {result,
  # post} AFTER. Compare structurally: headers (incl. Authorization / X-Amz-* set), request.path, method,
  # Host, Content-Type/Content-Length, body. Identity (result===post) holds but is not the graded contract;
  # the graded contract is the deep value of the mutated request.

SCOPE
  IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly): the entire SigV4 pipeline above — construction/defaulting,
    matchHost inference, getDateTime ISO transform, credentialString, canonicalString (path+query
    canonicalization, encodeRfc3986Full, bodyHash selection), canonicalHeaders/signedHeaders INCLUDING
    THE INCLUDE/IGNORE DESYNC, stringToSign, the kDate->kRegion->kService->kCredentials signing-key
    derivation and final HMAC, authHeader assembly, signQuery query injection, formatPath. The
    HEADERS_TO_IGNORE set {authorization, connection, x-amzn-trace-id, user-agent, expect,
    presigned-expires, range} is a SHORT algorithmic constant transcribed inline (NOT carried data —
    7 entries, no published-authority table). All AWS service/region special-cases (s3, ses/email,
    sdb, es/aoss swap, s3- prefix, isSingleRegion list, .cn) are inline algorithmic constants.

  CARRIED DATA: NONE. The SigV4 constants ('AWS4-HMAC-SHA256', 'aws4_request', the date format, the
    encodeRfc3986 escape set !'()*, the HEADERS_TO_IGNORE map, the s3/ses/es special-casing) are all
    short algorithmic literals reproduced inline above — there is no large published-authority table to
    extract. NO carried.json is written for this unit.

  OUT-OF-CONTRACT / OUT-OF-SCOPE (excluded from genInputs; documented for completeness):
    - request given as a STRING (url.parse) — not codec-faithful / not in envelope.
    - Buffer or non-string body — Buffer.byteLength + hash differ; non-round-trippable via JSON codec.
    - credentials omitted/falsy — reads process.env (ENV seam) — non-deterministic.
    - no pinned date in the relevant slot — reads new Date() (CLOCK seam) — non-deterministic.
    - isCodeCommitGit path (service codecommit + method 'GIT') — niche; datetime Z-strip + empty bodyHash.
    - The LRU credentialsCache is a pure memoization of kCredentials and is BEHAVIOR-NEUTRAL (asserted by
      running with cold/warm cache: identical signatures). Not a state seam for the contract.
    - undefined / NaN / boxed header values — not codec-faithful; behavior documented but never emitted.

